Article 2 (Amendment of Quantum Cluster Development Plans and Revocation of Designation) The term "documents prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Science and ICT" in the latter part of Article 26 (2) of the Act on the Promotion of Quantum Science and Technology and Quantum Industry (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following documents for the respective categories:
1. Where an amendment to a quantum cluster development plan under Article 25 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "quantum cluster development plan") is requested:
(a) A document stating the matters proposed to be amended in the quantum cluster development plan and the reasons for the amendment;
(b) Documents, including materials and drawings, capable of explaining the matters proposed to be amended in the quantum cluster development plan;
(c) Documents concerning the formulation and execution of the budget relating to the quantum cluster development plan.
2. Where revocation of the designation of a quantum cluster is requested:
(a) Documents, including materials and drawings, explaining the name, location, and area of the quantum cluster for which revocation is sought and the reasons for requesting revocation;
(b) Documents describing expected problems arising from revocation of the designation of the quantum cluster and measures for managing them;
(c) Documents concerning the formulation and execution of the budget relating to the quantum cluster development plan.
